Forvo is the place to hear&nbsp;all the words in the world pronounced by native speakers. Launched in 2008 and recognized in the&nbsp;[New York Times' 2013 "50 Best Sites of the Year"](https://techland.time.com/2013/05/06/50-best-websites-2013/slide/forvo/), it now hosts over&nbsp;**7 million words**&nbsp;in&nbsp;**450+ languages**, recorded by&nbsp;**1 million users**, and attracts&nbsp;**175 million visits annually.**

The system is simple: anyone can register, select their native language, and start recording pronunciations for others to hear. Content is community-driven and largely self-regulated. While some languages have more recordings than others, Forvo is still a versatile tool that can be woven into different language-learning routines.

That being said, I do believe the app still has significant UX potential waiting to be explored.
